            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Section 704(a) of Title VII prohibits the use of third\u2011party reprisals as a method of retaliation against a person who complained to the EEOC or otherwise opposed discrimination."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-87541634de57-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "To succeed on a retaliation claim, a plaintiff must show that discrimination occurred with respect to the individual who engaged in a protected activity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-87541634de57-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States (Amicus), according to United States (Amicus), the United States amicus brief argues that an employee who is fired because a relative or close associate filed an EEOC charge may sue under Title VII even though the employee himself did not engage in protected activity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Latherow",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-87541634de57-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Ms. Latherow contends that the term \u201caggrieved\u201d under Title VII should be read to include any person who claims to have been injured, mirroring the Fair Housing Act\u2019s definition."
      }
    ],
